                <pb facs="0661" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v04/pg623"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Senate bill 2370, authorizing the sale of certain vessels to Brazil for use in
                    the Brazilian coastwise shipping trade, was introduced on July 13, 1953;
                    companion bill 6317 was introduced in the House of Representatives on July 15,
                    1953. For text of statements made before the House Merchant Marine and Fisheries
                    Committee in support of the bills by Assistant Secretary Woodward and Officer in Charge of
                    Transportation <pb facs="0662" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/> and Communications
                    Policy Charles P. Nolan on March 24 and
                    June 8, 1954, respectively, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, April 5, 1954, pages 533–534, and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid</hi>., June 21, 1954, pages 951–953. Senate bill 2370 became Public
                    Law 496, approved July 15, 1954; for text, see 68 Stat. 481.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
